    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.extra, mini.pick\n\n### Description\n\n`:marks` prints \"mark line  col file/text\", file for globals, text for buffer-locals. right now, the picker diverges from vim in 3 ways: a) it prints path first then line and column numbers last, b) it doesn't print line text for buffer marks, which makes it hard to identify the desired item (admittedly easily rectified by pressing Tab, but still), and c) the items are smushed together and hard to read. it'd be nice if the output would have the same order as and similar formatting to `:marks`, and the line text for buffer marks.\n\neither grep-like:\n\n```text\n-- │ %5d:%-3d │\n\nA │     4:1   │ ~/.config/nvim-repro/init.lua\na │     4:1   │ local clone_cmd = { \"git\", \"clone\", \"--depth=1\", \"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim\", mini_path }\n```\n\nor vim-like (minus the bars):\n\n```text\n-- │ %5d │ %3d │\n\nA │     4 │   1 │ ~/.config/nvim-repro/init.lua\na │     4 │   1 │ local clone_cmd = { \"git\", \"clone\", \"--depth=1\", \"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim\", mini_path }\n```",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-06T08:25:29Z",
