        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nAligning `MiniExtra.pickers.marks` with `:marks` is not a design goal.\n\n> a) it prints path first then line and column numbers last, ...\n\nThis aligns it with other pickers that show location in some path. Like `MiniPick.builtin.grep`.\n\n> b) it doesn't print line text for buffer marks, which makes it hard to identify the desired item (admittedly easily rectified by pressing Tab, but still)\n\nYes, pressing `<Tab>` is indeed the suggested solution. I don't really like the inconsistency between buffer and non-buffer marks that this will introduce.\n\n> c) the items are smushed together and hard to read.\n\nThis also aligns with how location is displayed in other pickers. The idea is to have this as compact as possible to save horizontal space.\n\nWith this amount of adjustment, I think it might be better to write a custom picker for marks (the reference code is [here](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/6f0cd5049f414932ba55a5d6f3282a59d55c71a3/lua/mini/extra.lua#L1311-L1330) and is pretty concise). Assigning the picker to `MiniPick.registry.marks` (*after* `require('mini.extra').setup()` takes effect) will override the `marks` picker from 'mini.extra' and will be used when calling `:Pick marks`.",
            "created_at": "2026-10-06T08:25:29Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/2571#issuecomment-6012369492",
